59
00:01:57,419 --> 00:01:58,939
For a few years, the tree grows

60
00:01:58,839 --> 00:02:01,899
fast. By September 2000, Rosie's thousand dollars

61
00:02:01,799 --> 00:02:04,139
has grown to $2,123.

62
00:02:05,292 --> 00:02:08,032
Mia's virtual pet, meanwhile, has died. Eleven

63
00:02:07,932 --> 00:02:08,452
times.

64
00:02:09,166 --> 00:02:11,826
Then a storm hits. Lots of internet

65
00:02:11,726 --> 00:02:13,966
companies that everybody was excited about turn

66
00:02:13,866 --> 00:02:15,226
out to be worth almost nothing.

67
00:02:15,822 --> 00:02:18,022
Stocks fall for two whole years. By

68
00:02:17,922 --> 00:02:20,482
October 2002, Rosie's tree is down to

69
00:02:20,382 --> 00:02:21,602
$1,117.

70
00:02:22,742 --> 00:02:24,501
Told you. Money trees are scary.

71
00:02:25,127 --> 00:02:27,640
Ben pats Fort Cookie. Still one thousand

72
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:29,207
