73
00:02:29,781 --> 00:02:31,641
And for the first time, Nickel squawks

74
00:02:31,541 --> 00:02:31,761
it.

75
00:02:32,353 --> 00:02:33,613
Don't chop the tree!

76
00:02:34,345 --> 00:02:36,965
Here's the thing about storms. Rosie's companies

77
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:39,984
didn't disappear. People still bought food, shoes

78
00:02:40,145 --> 00:02:42,565
and medicine. The leaves fell, but the

79
00:02:42,465 --> 00:02:43,225
roots were fine.

80
00:02:44,751 --> 00:02:47,171
Rosie doesn't chop. Slowly, the tree grows

81
00:02:47,071 --> 00:02:50,930
back. By October 2007, it's worth $2,464.

82
00:02:52,271 --> 00:02:54,031
Then comes the biggest storm in eighty

83
00:02:53,931 --> 00:02:54,351
years.

84
00:02:55,021 --> 00:02:56,620
Banks had lent too much money to

85
00:02:56,521 --> 00:02:58,241
